| The Google Chat server (#1016): one Google Chat app, its events pulled from its Pub/Sub subscription (Google's REST clients, `google.golang.org/api`; outbound, no public address): `message.received` (filters `space`, `text`, `direct`; with its text) and `question.answered` (filters `space`, `question`), each with its `sender` (the Google Chat user, name and email) for a channel link, #1762; `list_spaces`, `send_message` and `ask_question` (a card with a button per option, marked answered after the first press); the messaging contract's `list_conversations`, `read_messages` (#4342: a space's history with `chat.app.messages.readonly`, else what the server kept for a day) and `reply` (#4345: the person's reply from the Messages page, as the Chat app); the service account key `GOOGLE_CHAT_CREDENTIALS` and `GOOGLE_CHAT_SUBSCRIPTION` in the secrets; Agent Loops on the Mac carries it, every Linux host installs it, and the catalogue lists it as `agents/googlechat` in the Agent Loops marketplace | agents | built | Tools, Events | 2026-11-10, against a fake Pub/Sub and Chat API only (`Go/internal/googlechatmcp`) | `Go/cmd/googlechat-mcp/main.go`, `Go/internal/googlechatmcp` | a real Workspace account and Chat app; the channel's name in the link card (#1762) is "Googlechat" until the clients name it |
